WEBVTT

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:39.320
It certainly is bad news keep me advised worse than anything we imagined Marling is dead and the police say Martin killed him

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.460
Boy, that's nonsense after having saved his life a dozen times

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:44.460
Oh Martin says a man named Blinker did it

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:50.280
But the police found a phonograph record of Martin's conversation with Marling just before he shot him including the gunshot

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:56.070
Police arrested Martin, but he escaped in the police car and is trying to capture Blinker with the police right behind him

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.360
You haven't brought the records with you.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:10.710
They're safely hidden.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.980
Tell you where, after you give me the money I need.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.930
You will tell me before I give you the money.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.030
Delay is dangerous.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.320
If the police get me, they would also get the record.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.620
I'm sure you would not like that.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.900
You seem to hold all the aces.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.500
Now, tell me where you have hidden them.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.570
In the safest possible place.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:39.590
Check room.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:41.590
A very clever hiding place.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.350
Have you brought the claim check with you?

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:45.520
And the jewelry?

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:46.340
Of course.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:49.550
You will not need any money, Blinker.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:59.800
Sorry you did that, Trudy.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.420
I wanted to question him.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:04.290
Stay where you are with your hands up.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:05.920
What happened, Trudy?

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.960
I just shot the man who abducted Marling

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.730
and caught the one who killed him.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.040
I don't think you really believe I'm guilty, do you, Trudy?

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.580
The police say they have proof.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.300
If I can search that man, I think I can prove they're wrong.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.300
Don't try to come in.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.510
Sorry, Trudy, I've got to search him.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:27.580
Got a very good shot, Trudy.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:35.820
forget that I know how to count. You fired three shots at Blanker and two at me. The gun's empty.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.160
I don't blame you for what you did, Trudy, if you're firmly convinced I'm guilty of murder and treason.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:45.290
I don't want to believe it, Jack, but we all love Marling, and I can't take a chance with treason.

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:49.720
By the way, how did Blanker happen to come here? He brought some jewelry I ordered. Janet knows.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.840
That's right, Jack. It's a shame you had to shoot the man that killed Marling.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:59.980
Can't talk now, and he was one of the black samurai. He threatened me, so I pretend to get money from my...

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.860
and I shot him before he killed me.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:13.180
Is this what he brought you?

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:13.660
Yes.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.280
Does this mean anything?

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:17.740
Check room ticket.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.440
It would be a perfect place to leave any incriminating evidence.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:21.690
It's 100 to 1.

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.310
It won't help me, but anything's worth trying.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:27.900
Please, open up.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:29.970
Look, let them in until I'm well.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:37.600
The door's locked and the key's gone.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.040
I'll open one of the other doors.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:42.070
Open up!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:44.890
Well, I guess we'll have to break it in.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:45.830
In this way.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:56.840
Did Martin do this?

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:58.310
No, I didn't.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:04:59.970
I heard Martin talking a little...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.840
When we arrive, where is he?

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:02.980
He left when he heard you hammering.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.910
We're stuck. He took our car and the keys to this one.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:40.330
Could you tell me who this is and why you killed him?

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:44.280
His name is Blinker. He came to collect for some jewelry.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.090
He said he was leaving the islands tonight.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.650
I suspected he was wanted by you, so I hesitated.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:51.070
He threatened me.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.580
Looks so good for Jack.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:57.380
There must be some way we could help him.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.790
Yes, Jack.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:10.530
Are you sure that's wise?

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.270
We will if you want us to.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:17.980
Let's hope so.

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:20.580
Bye.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:27.220
He says he wants us to bring the police to the boat where Marling was murdered.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:28.910
He thinks he can prove he's innocent.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:31.850
He didn't say, but he seemed pretty sure.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.360
Coming along, Trudy?

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:34.550
I don't think I'd better.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:35.730
He might not want me.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:38.110
Trudy, you must forget what happened last night.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.450
Jack would really be offended if he knew how you feel.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:42.380
All right, I'll get my thing.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:51.910
This is the box that Blanca left at the checkroom.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.560
I opened it in front of the attendant so that I could verify its contents.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.500
If these papers are on the level, it'll run the Black Samurai out of Honolulu.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.380
What about these phonograph records?

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.080
These, I hope, will prove my innocence.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:04.570
Listen to this.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:24.800
...to find the Fraulein as a man, huh?

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:38.260
I'm trusting people, Marling.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:40.920
I've got your secret, and after I get rid of you,

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.040
I'm selling it to the nation, paying the most for it,

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:45.150
whether the black samurai likes it or not.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:46.360
Thanks, Marling.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:47.480
So long.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.760
Meantime, listen to what I really said to Marling.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.600
by the morning, and the mandate's secret will be in Tokyo.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.440
Well, that proves Jack didn't shoot him.

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:34.470
Of course I didn't.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.770
As a matter of fact, the bullet that killed him was meant for me.

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:38.990
Well, I admit it looks a little brighter for you,

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:41.150
but what I want to know is how they got that other record of you,

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:42.630
telling him you were going to let him have it.

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:44.750
You were here last night. Did you notice this?

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:46.230
Yes, but I didn't know what it was.

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:48.410
Well, it's an elaboration on American invention.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.820
With it, you can use the record of any man's voice

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:54.180
and reproduce that voice speaking with any words you care to substitute.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:55.840
Here, let me show you.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:08:59.970
Now, when I turn on this record, say...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.700
Anything you want to say, but don't speak out loud.

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:02.620
Just mild the words.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:10.050
The Mandarin secret, Marling, you are no more use to me,

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:11.690
so I'll put you out of the way.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.810
That's enough. I'm sold.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.220
Does that mean Jack's free?

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:18.160
Well, not exactly.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:19.900
You'll have to demonstrate this to the chief.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.280
Of course, that's a mere formality.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:23.300
You know how glad we all are, don't you?

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:24.120
You better be.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:26.250
I hope I'm forgiven for last night.

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:29.720
I'm leaving for Chongqing tomorrow, and I'd hate to part bad friends.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.960
Beating for Shung King without witnessing the signing of the Mandan Treaty?

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.370
How can you have it signed now that Marling is dead?

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.920
Well Wu Tan automatically becomes his successor.

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:39.630
Well, you've got to stay, Trudy.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:41.350
Naturally, if the pact is to be signed.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.620
While you people go to police headquarters,

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:45.560
I've got to get this part of the story on the wire.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:37.110
murdered Marling. We can use that to convince the Mandanese. It is we who are

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:42.650
their real friends. Of course. Have an agent fly the news demand and demand the

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:46.230
release of their Japanese prisoners. Shall I have him bring out the prisoners?

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:51.420
No, have him stay there with them. They can act as our agents. And by the way,

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:55.680
another thing, tell him to take along a portable shortwave set so we can keep in

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:56.140
touch with them.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:18.760
By accession to this seal, through the death of my friend and master, Ma Ling,

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:21.220
I am empowered to sign for Man Don.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.500
Now prepare to receive the secret of Man Don.

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:42.420
yes cablegram has just been delivered for captain wink uh bring it in thank you if you'll permit me

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:51.230
certainly concerns us all it's from general kai ling man don has heard the story of marling's

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:55.730
death at captain martin's hands they repudiate their treaty and order wu-tan to return

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:59.970
and show cause why they should not give the secret route to the japanese but martin has been

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:02.260
I'll cable Mandan.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.260
Mandan is an isolated province.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:05.620
There is no telegraph.

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:08.370
The quickest means of communication is by plane.

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:10.570
Well, I guess that leaves it squarely up to me.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:14.360
I'll have to fly you back to Mandan and prove my innocence in your courts.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.340
Isn't that risky?

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.220
How can you be sure that you can convince them?

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.900
Same way I convinced the police here.

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:20.720
I have the original record at my hotel.

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:23.640
When the Lausanne hears it, you will know the truth.

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:27.080
With the testimony of the rest of your party, that ought to be conclusive.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:29.970
Unfortunately, I've been ordered back to Chongqing by General...

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.880
I'm sorry, but my boss has ordered me back, too.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:35.080
He says I've taken too long on this story as it is.

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:37.730
I think Tommy and I can verify Jack's story.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:38.730
Nothing doing, Janet.

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:41.030
No use of you two risking your neck because I have to.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:41.610
But Jack...

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:42.970
Sorry, Tommy, I got into this alone.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:43.970
That's the way I'll get out of it.

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:46.190
You and Janet better go back to Shung King with Wing.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:48.160
How soon can you arrange a plane for me?

00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:50.380
You're practically on your way to Mandunnel.

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:59.060
Manalulo, two days late find the date.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:13.770
Where would our Fraulein's plans be now if I had not ordered our envoy to take a radio with him when he flew into Mandon?

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:19.360
Contact Krishimi in Mandon, quickly.

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:28.330
DBS calling Mandon. DBS calling Mandon.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:34.580
TBS calling Mandan. Come in, Mandan.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:36.980
Mandan answering TBS.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:38.900
Go ahead, TBS.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:41.330
Kageyama speaking.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:46.250
Martin is flying to Mandan with treaties signed by United Nations.

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:49.210
He may prove to Lausanne he did not kill Ma Ling.

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:51.590
Devour Anno. Intercept him in plane.

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:54.000
Make sure he does not reach Mandan.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:59.560
It shall be done. One moment, please.

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:11.900
The plane is settling to land. It may be Martin's.

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:15.510
Phoebe, you fool, it must be. Go to the Lausanne at once.

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:18.260
If he believes Martin's story, tell him.

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.370
But that will stop China from getting it.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:23.540
We must act quickly.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:35.060
It is good to be home once more.

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:36.300
That may be good for you,

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:38.280
but if this record doesn't convince the Losan,

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:39.360
it won't be so good for me.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:40.700
The Losan will be convinced.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:41.700
I have heard the record.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:57.690
I welcome the coming of the new governor to his people.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:14:59.960
I am...

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:04.740
But I did not expect to find you with the enemies of Mandan.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:09.540
And I did not expect to find you with the murderer of Marling.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:14.030
He did not kill Marling. He came here to stand trial in our court.

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:16.880
Prove the Japanese bore false witness against him.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:20.300
He has come to deceive you, as he did Marling and Bhutan.

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:25.020
When I feel your opinion is of value, I shall ask for it.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.010
Did he bring proof?

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:28.850
Conclusive proof, your highness.

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:29.970
The black samurai...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.220
I killed Ma Ling and manufactured evidence

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:33.260
to throw the blame on me.

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:36.360
But there was a record made that tells the true story.

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:38.060
A record?

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:41.620
The Occidentals have a device for catching and holding

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:42.620
sound forever.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:46.340
On this, I recorded the last words of Ma Ling

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:47.460
as he died in my arms.

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:59.980
If I can check in one point.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:01.550
This isn't the record.

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:04.260
The Japanese must have stolen it and replaced it with this.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.200
It was Mao Ling speaking.

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:08.370
Let me hear the rest of it.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:11.170
But this is the record manufactured to prove Captain Martin guilty.

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:13.230
It was the record he brought as proof.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:14.550
Let him submit it.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:15.360
Continue.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:23.980
and the Fraulein's a man, huh?

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:39.180
That's what comes from trusting people, Marling.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.150
Now I've got your secret.

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:45.140
And after I get rid of you, I'm selling it to the nation, paying the most for it.

00:16:45.610 --> 00:16:47.610
whether the black samurai likes it or not.

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:49.850
Thanks, Marley, and so long.

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:54.050
Does your highness require further proof?

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:57.380
After what I have heard.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.400
Do you still deny your guilt?

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.780
I certainly do.

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:03.700
When a man protests his innocence...

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:05.890
Men down law cannot punish him.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:08.370
But he must undergo the mend on ordeal.

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:11.340
If he comes through alive, he is free.

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:13.520
For he has proved his innocence.

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:16.120
Is there any chance of my coming through alive?

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.720
for one who is not of our faith.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.480
The chances are very remote.

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:24.000
And if I refuse to submit, the penalty is death.

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:27.580
All right.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:30.000
I'll submit to your ordeal under one con-

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.300
condition.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:34.500
And that is, if I don't survive, you will give the men in secret to China.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:35.760
Your Highness.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:38.500
Would the murderer of Ma Ling make such a request?

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:40.780
It seems improbable.

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:44.950
A clever man, however guilty, might make such a request.

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:47.020
knowing it would suggest his innocence.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:49.840
I cannot forget the record.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:53.340
You must undergo the ordeal without reservation.

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:57.910
I shall hold you responsible for the prisoner until tomorrow.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:10.790
Just what is the ordeal?

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:14.980
There will be plenty of time to explain that to you before tomorrow.

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:23.720
Thank you.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.980
Thank you.

00:18:31.690 --> 00:18:31.890
We're done.

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:33.610
Go through our test ordeal.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.860
If you will confess your guilt.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:38.180
I did not kill Ma Ling.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:43.320
I find myself praying this test will prove your words are true.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:45.020
Thanks.

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:54.560
at any point.

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:56.600
By admitting your guilt.

00:19:37.030 --> 00:19:38.270
Time to confess.

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:39.700
Thank you.

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.540
There's not much time left to confess.

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:09.460
There's more time than I need.

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:05.640
Have you heard him, Jack?

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:07.240
I thought it null.

00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:08.620
I've just come from Wayne.

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:12.120
All we know is that Jack and Wu-Tan arrived safely in Mandar.

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:15.260
I wish we'd gone with him instead of coming back here to Chongqing.

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:16.420
So do I.

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:18.940
wing now.

00:22:21.370 --> 00:22:21.610
Hello?

00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:23.150
Oh.

00:22:24.310 --> 00:22:24.630
Judy.

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:25.490
No!

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:27.090
Yes.

00:22:28.340 --> 00:22:29.980
Well, Wing will call me the moment he gets Jack.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:30.460
next report.

00:22:31.690 --> 00:22:32.810
Well, when will we be seeing you?

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:34.640
I'm stuck at the office, Haley.

